+Olympic designs
+The Olympic Insignia Protection Act 1987 allows the Registrar of Designs to approve forms to:
+- register an olympic design
+- extend or reduce a registered olympic design's protection period
+- amend the Register of Olympic Designs
+- respond to an application to register an olympic design
+- respond to an application to extend a protection period.
+A fee applies to some forms. For more information, including how to file and make a payment, visit the Olympic designs.
